  <!-- 
  ==============================================================================
  IMPORTANT NOTES & BEST PRACTICES
  ==============================================================================
  
  SITEMAP INDEX RULES:
  - Can contain up to 50,000 sitemap references
  - Each sitemap file can have up to 50,000 URLs
  - Maximum sitemap file size: 50MB (uncompressed)
  - Can use gzip compression (recommended for large sitemaps)
  - All URLs must be from the same domain/subdomain
  
  MAINTENANCE TASKS:
  1. Update lastmod timestamps when sitemaps are regenerated
  2. Add new sitemap files as content grows
  3. Remove obsolete sitemap files
  4. Verify all sitemap URLs are accessible (200 status)
  5. Test with Google Search Console sitemap report
  6. Monitor indexing coverage and errors
  
  AUTOMATION RECOMMENDATIONS:
  - Auto-generate sitemaps when content is published
  - Update lastmod dates automatically
  - Use server-side scripts or CMS plugins
  - Set up cron jobs for periodic regeneration
  - Notify search engines of updates via ping
  
  DEPLOYMENT CHECKLIST:
  ✓ Replace 'your-domain.com' with actual domain
  ✓ Create all referenced sitemap files
  ✓ Verify all sitemap URLs return 200 status
  ✓ Test XML validity
  ✓ Add to robots.txt: Sitemap: https://your-domain.com/sitemap-index.xml
  ✓ Submit to Google Search Console
  ✓ Submit to Bing Webmaster Tools
  ✓ Monitor crawl stats and coverage
  
  SEARCH ENGINE PING URLS (Optional - for automatic updates):
  - Google: http://www.google.com/ping?sitemap=https://your-domain.com/sitemap-index.xml
  - Bing: http://www.bing.com/ping?sitemap=https://your-domain.com/sitemap-index.xml
  
  TROUBLESHOOTING:
  - Error "Couldn't fetch sitemap": Check URL accessibility
  - Error "Invalid XML": Validate with online XML validators
  - Low indexing: Check for robots.txt blocks, canonicals, redirects
  - Slow crawling: Verify server response times, check crawl budget
  
  PERFORMANCE TIPS:
  ✓ Compress sitemaps with gzip (saves bandwidth)
  ✓ Use CDN for sitemap hosting (faster access)
  ✓ Cache sitemaps (reduce server load)
  ✓ Split large sitemaps by date or category
  ✓ Use absolute URLs (never relative)
  
  ACCELLAX 361° SPECIFIC NOTES:
  - Only public marketing pages included
  - All private/sensitive content excluded (dashboards, kid data, etc.)
  - COPPA/GDPR compliant (no personal data in sitemaps)
  - Mobile app download pages included for discovery
  - Blog/help content for SEO and user education
  
  ==============================================================================
  END OF SITEMAP INDEX - AccellaX 361°
  ==============================================================================
  -->

